        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "EO 11355 (1967-05-26, 32 FR 7803) amends EO 10647 of November 28, 1955 on appointments under the Defense Production Act of 1950: clause 1 rewrites the first sentence of subsection 305(a) (annual survey by the Chairman of the Civil Service Commission of appointments under section 710(b)(1) of the Act), clause 2 rewrites paragraph (1) of subsection 305(b) (the statistical report) and clause 3 revokes Part II of EO 10647. I read the full held Federal Register text (jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_11355.txt, 32 FR 7803, PDF pages 7-7) and confirmed its number, title and date against the census register; the three numbered clauses are the complete inventory, and the opening authority paragraph is a lead-in, not a command. EO 12919 (signed 1994-06-03) supersedes or revokes EO 10647 and EO 11355 by number in section 904(a), and the dossier carries the ACT record for it. The first end of every clause is that express revocation. Under the owner ruling of 2026-10-21 on strike-and-insert amendments each amending clause continues, amended, until the parent order ends; EO 10647 ended by the same section on the same date. EO 12107 (signed 1978-12-28) later substituted Office of Personnel Management words in EO 11355 and is recorded as a later event of clause 1, not an end. Bounded search read for this order: the dossier's three machine searches (U.S. Code release point 119-121 through 2026-10-09; eCFR and GovInfo CFR bulk through 2026-10-14; Federal Register catalog disposition notes and operative sentences of 17,521 saved order texts), after reading their coverage notes, which carry no coverage warning; the Cruden by-number scan of held order texts in the packet's LOOKUPS.md; and a full read of EO 12553 (held FR text, 33,227 characters).\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"Own terms: none; the order has no sunset or condition. The only later instruments held that touch this order are EO 12107 (an amendment by word substitution effective 1979-01-01, recorded as a later event) and EO 12919 (the revocation). The Federal Register catalog note on EO 11355 lists exactly those two. No held source shows EO 10647 or the Defense Production Act appointment authority ending before 1994-06-03; the amended sections' own ending is therefore not shown earlier.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"Independent commands: clauses 1 and 2 only rewrite subsections of EO 10647, and clause 3 revokes a Part of EO 10647; the order creates no appointment, fund or delegation of its own. EO 10647 itself ended by the same section of EO 12919, so no command survives apart from the order.\",\"savings_check\":\"Savings: section 903 of EO 12919 preserves the validity of things done under earlier assignments of authority; the amended commands themselves are revoked by name.\",\"scope_check\":\"Whole-order scope: EO 12919 section 904(a) lists EO 11355 in full, without an 'in part' limit, so all three clauses end on the same date. EO 12107 amends clause 1 only by substitution and does not end any clause.\"}",
